EXPERIMENT 51 – REGRESSION TESTING OF LOGIN AND LOGOUT USING SELENIUM
AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to implement regression testing of the login and logout functionality.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Create ChromeDriver and WebDriverWait with a timeout of 10 seconds.
3. Login using valid credentials and verify the Products page.
4. Open the menu and click Logout.
5. Verify that the login button is displayed again.
6. Run the script after every application change to detect defects.
7. Close the browser.
CODE
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.ExpectedConditions;
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.WebDriverWait;
import java.time.Duration;

public class Exercise51 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(
                driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));

            driver.get("https://www.saucedemo.com");

            driver.findElement(By.id("user-name"))
                .sendKeys("standard_user");

            driver.findElement(By.id("password"))
                .sendKeys("secret_sauce");

            driver.findElement(By.id("login-button")).click();

            String heading = wait.until(
                ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(
                    By.className("title"))).getText();

            System.out.println("Login check : " +
                (heading.equals("Products") ? "PASS" : "FAIL"));

            driver.findElement(
                By.id("react-burger-menu-btn")).click();

            wait.until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(
                By.id("logout_sidebar_link"))).click();

            boolean loginVisible = wait.until(
                ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(
                    By.id("login-button"))).isDisplayed();

            System.out.println("Logout check : " +
                (loginVisible ? "PASS" : "FAIL"));

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- URL: https://www.saucedemo.com
- Username: standard_user
- Password: secret_sauce
OUTPUT
Login check : PASS
Logout check : PASS


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to implement regression testing of login and logout functionality was executed successfully, and the output was verified.
